{
    "attributes": {
        "action": "Increase Local Housing Allowance rates",
        "additional_details": "When the LHA was introduced in 2008, it covered 50% of private rental market properties in a given local area. If tenants secured a property priced below their designated LHA rate, they could be paid up \u00a315 per week.\r\n \r\nHowever, now only less 3% of properties cost low enough for the LHA rates to cover the full cost. We call on the Government to increase LHA rates so they cover 50% of local properties to reduce the chance of the families needing to rent them becoming homeless.",
        "background": "It is estimated that Local Housing Allowance rates cover less than 3% of advertised private rentals in England. However, it is estimated that around 45-50% of private renting households are claiming Universal Credit. ",
